For every study, return one result:
- source: the id in square brackets of the source you quote (an abstract or a ClinicalTrials.gov record);
- pmid: the PMID of the study;
- quote: one or two consecutive sentences copied exactly, character for character, from that source, that state the whole-sample result on the primary outcome; "" when the sources do not state it;
- result: positive (the primary outcome improved in the whole sample, in the direction of the claim) | null (no significant change) | negative (it worsened) | not_reported (the sources name the primary outcome but give no whole-sample result, or do not say which outcome is primary);
- endpoint: what the primary outcome measures: lifespan | healthspan | biomarker | disease | mechanism | unknown;
- human_rungs: for a study in humans, "human_markers" (laboratory and instrumental measures: blood markers, body composition, imaging) and/or "human_clinical" (function, frailty, pain, disease, mortality).
A registered primary outcome tells you which outcome is primary; the abstract may report its result. Do not report a subgroup or secondary result here. Do not use knowledge outside these sources.

